# What goes in the sdist, and why it is the whole tree.
#
# RELEASE.md §8 promises a distribution can retest from the sdist, and the suite
# reads the tree it lives in: `tests/data/` for the fixtures, `bench/results/` for the
# two artifacts a test pins, `tools/`, `demo/`, `pi-extension/src/` for sources it
# greps, and at least one `.yml` because the privacy walk floors every suffix it claims
# to read. An enumeration of those paths would be a second copy of the import graph,
# silently wrong the first time a test reads something new — so the manifest grafts the
# directories and lets the suite decide.
#
# `pi-extension/node_modules` is the one prune: 178 MB of installed packages that
# `npm ci` regenerates from the lockfile that does ship.
graft service
graft tests
graft bench
graft docs
graft tools
graft demo
graft data
graft spec
graft pi-extension
graft .github

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include ARCHITECTURE.md
include RELEASE.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include TODO.md
include LICENSE
include pyproject.toml

prune pi-extension/node_modules

global-exclude __pycache__
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude *.pyo
